---
// Part 1 — copy from "Copy update 28 Sept" (docs/), one 70ch column. Each of
// the doc's section breaks opens on a full-bleed <Scene>; the photographs are
// from Unsplash (credits in src/assets/story/README.md).
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Scene from '../components/Scene.astro';
import ReadProgress from '../components/ReadProgress.astro';
import fire from '../assets/story/problem-v2-01-fire.jpg';
import westminster from '../assets/story/problem-v2-02-westminster-dusk.jpg';
import twoSides from '../assets/story/problem-v2-03-two-sides.jpg';
import unionFlags from '../assets/story/problem-v2-04-union-flags.jpg';
---

<Layout
  title="The Real Problem — We The People"
  introLines={['The Real', 'Problem']}
  joinCollapsed
>
  <PageHero lines={['The Real', 'Problem']} />

  <ReadProgress />
  <article class="prose">
    <Scene
      first
      eager
      src={fire}
      alt="Smoke and flames pouring from the roof of a block of flats"
      heading="We all know things are going wrong. We all feel it."
    />

    <p class="lead">
      Like you, everyone has their own list of concerns: cost of living, inequality,
      immigration, war, the climate, the water, the trains, even potholes…
    </p>
    <p class="lead">Whatever we care about, so little gets done.</p>
    <p class="lead">
      We're left feeling let down, angry, afraid and like we don’t have the power to do
      anything about it.
    </p>

    <Scene
      src={westminster}
      alt="The Houses of Parliament in silhouette against a stormy evening sky"
      heading="We can’t trust politicians to fix anything."
    />
    <p>It’s not clear if any politicians put our interests first.</p>
    <p>Perhaps red-tape, finance and the global system make it near impossible.</p>
    <p>
      When things go wrong, we’re promised that we can elect someone different, someone
      better.
    </p>
    <p>But how often do we vote with high hopes, only to be let down?</p>
    <p>It’s no wonder trust in politicians – and our system – is at an all time low.</p>

    <Scene
      src={twoSides}
      alt="Two protests split down the middle: Stand Up To Racism placards on one side, St George's flags on the other"
      heading="Our real danger"
    />
    <p>This system failure couldn’t come at a worse time.</p>
    <p>
      Tech has made us lonelier and more disconnected. Our daily lives are getting tougher.
      And our media, old and new, profits by pitting us against one another.
    </p>
    <p>Politicians are the same. They pitch to one side or the other to gain power.</p>

    <h2>So we feel more divided than ever</h2>
    <p>Our democracy wasn’t designed for this.</p>
    <p>
      Our elections rely on the losers accepting defeat. But when we’re this fractured, we
      struggle to accept the policies brought in by the other side. Our differences are so
      deep, we can't work them out through the system any more.
    </p>
    <p>
      This kind of division has ushered in dictatorships or even led to civil war in other
      places, at other times.
    </p>

    <Scene
      src={unionFlags}
      alt="A crowd waving Union flags, arms raised and cheering"
      heading="But We The People still believe in democracy"
    />
    <p>
      We believe we can rediscover our ability to talk, listen and compromise no matter how
      difficult it seems right now.
    </p>
    <p>It will not happen through politicians, political parties or elections.</p>
    <p>We need something new.</p>

    <p class="pull">That is what this project is all about.</p>

    <a class="back" href="/hope">Our Real Hope →</a>
  </article>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    var back = document.querySelector('article.prose .back');
    if (!back) return;
    var fired = false;
    var observer = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      entries.forEach(function (entry) {
        if (entry.isIntersecting && !fired) {
          fired = true;
          window.posthog?.capture('problem_article_read');
          observer.disconnect();
        }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.5 });
    observer.observe(back);
  });
</script>
